    "status": "present",
    "value": "Each order has a duration and an arrival time. Orders are handled first come, first served (by arrival time, ties broken by their position in the input). With a given number of shoppers, each order is assigned to the shopper who becomes free earliest and starts at the later of its arrival time and that shopper's free time. An order's wait is its completion time minus its arrival time. Find the smallest number of shoppers for which the average wait over all orders is at most maxAverageWait, or return -1 if even one shopper per order cannot meet it."
  },
